# Template consistency

- This repo is a **C# / ASP.NET Core** example: server-rendered HTML + **GOV.UK Frontend** only. **No** React/Vue/Angular/Svelte or Blazor for UI.
- C# renderers track Frontend `template.njk`. Do not shell out to Node to render a request. Compare **C# HTML** to official fixtures for every fixture (primary gate); the Nunjucks check is freshness only. See [`docs/testing-components.md`](docs/testing-components.md).
- Priorities: frontend web performance → frontend security → reduced maintenance → accessibility → inclusive design.
- Keep [`AGENTS.md`](AGENTS.md) slim; put detail in [`docs/`](docs/README.md). Dual audience: see [`docs/documentation-structure.md`](docs/documentation-structure.md).
- Every feature or prompt-driven change must update dual-audience docs (humans + agents) in the right place — same change set as the code.
- Follow current C# and ASP.NET Core practice recorded in [`docs/tech-stack.md`](docs/tech-stack.md).
- Before upgrading Frontend: read https://github.com/alphagov/govuk-frontend/releases/latest then [`docs/upgrading-govuk-frontend.md`](docs/upgrading-govuk-frontend.md).
- Respect EditorConfig / Prettier / markdownlint; run `npm run verify:docs` after doc changes.
- 100% coverage (functions, branches, statements) for application code when it exists; never edit fixture `html` to pass tests.
- Serve pages and assets with [`baseline/`](baseline/) (cache kinds and OWASP headers). Compress with Brotli (`br`); Gzip is only the fallback when the client does not advertise `br`. Playbooks: [`docs/frontend-performance.md`](docs/frontend-performance.md), [`docs/frontend-security.md`](docs/frontend-security.md).
- Compile CSS with Sass (`styles/` → Frontend `@use` → `govuk-overrides.scss` last). Never use `!important` in service CSS. See [`docs/styles.md`](docs/styles.md).
- When work is complete, split it into focused commits with comprehensive messages.
